faiza-ps: Heads-up 1 Quantix Payments pilot next week. They surface a single HTTP/2 tunnel at the edge and want to multiplex ~150 logical streams. Key asks: Rust SDK mux example (they prefer Rust), consistent telemetry tags for their Datadog pipeline, ephemeral token rotation pattern, SOC2+ISO questionnaire path, and a rough hosted vs dedicated cost for short 5k QPS bursts (2-6 min). Can someone assemble a tiny runbook + snippets?

otto-sales: Demo Thurs 11am PT. They'll start on Hosted and may request Dedicated if jitter/latency is problematic. Need something we can hand to their infra team.

marin-eng: Notes on edge proxies: many HTTP/2 proxies at the edge will rewrite/strip upgrade or custom headers. If that happens, use header-based mux where stream_id is sent as an initial header and set transport_hint: "http2-proxy". Rust SDK example (minimal streaming + mux):
```rust
use redwood::Client;
use futures::StreamExt;

#[tokio::main]
async fn main() -> anyhow::Result<()> {
    let client = Client::new("$RW_KEY").with_mux(true).with_transport_hint("http2-proxy");
    let mut s1 = client.stream("gpt-4o-infer").stream_id("quantix-01").spawn().await?;
    tokio::spawn(async move {
        while let Some(chunk) = s1.next().await {
            println!("s1 chunk: {:?}", chunk);
        }
    });
    let mut s2 = client.stream("gpt-4o-infer").stream_id("quantix-02").spawn().await?;
    while let Some(c) = s2.next().await {
        println!("s2 chunk: {:?}", c);
    }
    Ok(())
}
```
Fallback: open independent short-lived connections per logical stream or use non-streaming batch endpoint.

marin-eng: Telemetry/labels: include service=quantix, env=pilot, stream_id, tenant_id, demo_run. If they use Datadog, also pass x-datadog-trace-id header so they can correlate. We ingest these when trace:true is enabled on the stream.

jem-devex: For structured output and tool calls, give them a small contract to validate parsing. Example function call schema we demo: 
```json
{"name":"extract_payment","params":{"type":"object","properties":{"merchant_id":{"type":"string"},"amount_usd":{"type":"number"},"currency":{"type":"string"}},"required":["merchant_id","amount_usd"]}}
```
Recommend they run 5-8 sample prompts through the contract locally and share the results with Optimize to catch regressions. I'll prepare a tiny validator script in Rust/Node to include in the runbook.

sec-bot: Compliance note 1: procurement should send SOC2 + ISO questionnaire PDFs to security@redwood.ai. Quick blockers: (1) a dataflow diagram showing what crosses our endpoints, (2) retention policy and whether raw utterances may contain PII, (3) if Dedicated requested provide KMS/HSM vendor details. Typical turnaround: 2-4 business days after we receive completed questionnaires and diagrams.

otto-sales: Pricing: they asked about 5k QPS short bursts 2-6 min multiple times/day. Any immediate ballpark for Hosted vs Dedicated?

marin-eng: For those bursty peaks two common options: (A) Hosted with negotiated burst credits for pilots (case-by-case), or (B) short-term Dedicated reservation sized to the peak. Ballpark Dedicated slice for that pattern is $12k-25k/mo depending on GPU family and acceptable quantization. For the demo we can offer a simulated 1.5k QPS 10-min run to collect metrics.

jem-devex: Operational checklist for the demo (short):
- Provision ephemeral API key scoped to demo workspace (rotate every 10-15m)
- Enable mux / transport_hint and set trace:true for correlation
- Share expected payload sizes and max_token length (we tune batch windows accordingly)
- If they want SAML SSO for test users, provide SP metadata and a test account early
- Send a 5-prompt validation set for structured output checks

faiza-ps: Can someone produce a one-page runbook + two snippets (Rust mux + curl fallback) by EOD Tue? I'll forward their procurement contact and any questionnaires when I get them.

marin-eng: I'll draft runbook and include a small async Rust load generator script to simulate multiplexed QPS and notes on kernel tuning (max_tokens, batch_window_ms).

jem-devex: I'll add the validator, structured output checklist, and a troubleshooting section: common edge issues (header stripping, max concurrent streams limits, 502+ proxy resets), token expiry handling (refresh dance), and payload size impacts on batching.

sec-bot: Confirmed 1 security will triage SOC2/ISO once questionnaire + dataflow arrive.

otto-sales: Scheduling: quick 30m sync Wed 8am PT to finalize runbook and pricing? :calendar:

faiza-ps: Works for me. Thanks team 680 I'll post initial payload shapes and their QPS histogram here in a minute.
